
To get OSDK built for MacOS (Tahoe 26.5.2), you must first use homebrew thus:

	$ brew install gcc-14 freeimage

Then 'make' .. and to install in a local OSDK directory:

	$ OSDK=/Users/<you>/Desktop/OSDK2.0/ make install # for example

.. and then, naturally,

	$ export OSDK=/Users/<you>/Desktop/OSDK2.0/
	# Or wherever you installed it ..

.. will give you a base path to the installed toolchain - set PATH accordingly, e.g.

	$ export PATH=$PATH:$OSDK/bin

Note:

	If OSDK is set, 'make' will attempt to install a build into it!
	Only set the OSDK variable after a complete, successful build.
	To build again, unset OSDK - i.e.
	
	$ export OSDK=
	$ make # etc.

